Package: metrodag
Title: Monotone Schematic Layouts for Directed Acyclic Graphs
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Hamid", "Bulut", email = "me@hamidbulut.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Draws causal directed acyclic graphs (DAGs) for epidemiology and
    causal inference as publication figures in a schematic metro-map style.
    A deterministic layered layout in the tradition of Sugiyama, Tagawa and
    Toda (1981) <doi:10.1109/TSMC.1981.4308636> places variables and routes
    arrows along vertical and diagonal tracks; labels, arrowheads and station
    clearances are measured on the output device so exported figures stay
    legible at manuscript sizes. Analysis roles (exposure, outcome, adjusted,
    unobserved) annotate the same fixed geometry across analysis views, and
    adjustment sets can optionally be checked with 'dagitty', the R interface
    to 'DAGitty' described by Textor et al. (2016) <doi:10.1093/ije/dyw341>.
    Figures are drawn with 'ggplot2'; layout computation is separate from
    rendering and reports quantitative readability metrics.
